1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:07,740
The art of persuasion means convincing others to agree with your point of view or to follow your course of action.
说服的艺术，就是劝服他人认同你的观点，或者遵循你的行动方案。

2
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:14,910
For some of us, persuasion is an instinctive quality and the power of influencing comes naturally.
对我们当中的一些人来说，说服力是一种出于本能的特质，影响他人的能力也是与生俱来的。

3
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:20,400
For the rest of us, persuasion skills can be learned and developed over time.
而对我们当中其余的人来说，说服技能可以随着时间的推移习得和培养。

4
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:28,890
Employers place a great value on employees with persuasion skills because they can impact several aspects of job performance.
雇主非常看重具备说服技能的员工，因为这些技能能够影响工作表现的多个方面。

5
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:34,940
Besides, teamwork and leadership rely heavily on the power of persuasion to get things done.
此外，团队合作和领导力在很大程度上依靠说服力来把事情办成。

6
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:44,490
Without persuasion skills, employees may not be as committed to or convinced of the importance of an organization’s vision and long-term mission.
如果缺乏说服技能，员工可能就不会那么坚定地拥护组织的愿景和长期使命，也不会那么确信其重要性。

7
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:54,210
Effective use of persuasion skills will not only help get your coworkers excited about your ideas but also help you motivate them to achieve a common goal.
有效运用说服技能，不仅有助于让同事对你的想法充满热情，还有助于你激励他们去实现共同的目标。

8
00:00:55,010 --> 00:01:01,790
In order to learn the art of persuasion in the workplace, you need to understand how to handle conflicts and reach agreements.
要学会职场中的说服艺术，你需要懂得如何处理冲突、达成一致。

9
00:01:02,590 --> 00:01:09,000
Good communication is the first step in effective persuasion, but logic and reasoning are just as important.
良好的沟通是有效说服的第一步，但逻辑和推理同样重要。

10
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:15,460
Before you can get somebody on board with your goal, you should help them understand why they should pursue it.
要想让别人支持你的目标，你应该先帮助他们明白为什么应该追求这一目标。

11
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:28,470
Using visual aids to back up your ideas can help communicate your ideas better and make compelling arguments so your listeners will come to a logical choice and become fully committed to your ideas and plans.
用视觉辅助工具来佐证你的想法，有助于更好地传达这些想法、提出令人信服的论点，从而让听众做出合乎逻辑的选择，并全心全意地拥护你的想法和计划。

12
00:01:29,270 --> 00:01:37,120
Successful persuasion skills are based on your ability to have positive interactions and maintain meaningful relationships with people.
成功的说服技能，建立在你与人积极互动、维系有意义关系的能力之上。

13
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:43,360
In order to sustain those relationships, you must be able to work in their best interests as well.
为了维系这些关系，你也必须能够从他们的最大利益出发去做事。

14
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:48,400
Your coworkers are more likely to agree with you when they succeed alongside you.
同事和你一起取得成功时，就更有可能认同你。

15
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:54,550
The more they achieve and the greater progress they make, the more they trust your judgement and strength.
他们取得的成就越多、进步越大，就越信任你的判断力和实力。

16
00:01:55,350 --> 00:02:00,410
We persuade and get persuaded every day—we’re either convincing or being convinced.
我们每天都在说服别人，也在被别人说服——不是在劝服别人，就是在被别人劝服。

17
00:02:01,210 --> 00:02:11,170
A vast majority of people prefer collaboration and teamwork over traditional organizational structures; no one likes to be told what to do or to be pushed around.
绝大多数人更喜欢协作和团队合作，而不是传统的组织结构；没有人喜欢听别人吩咐自己该做什么，也没有人喜欢被人摆布。

18
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:18,270
Therefore, organizations and leaders should use powerful persuasion skills to bring about necessary changes.
因此，组织和领导者应该运用强有力的说服技能来促成必要的变革。
